Z||000011||FIERO JOHN-WI||11-21-2001||03:26 PM||||Hey fellow wing less fiero owners, just a little fact for you collector or hobbiests of fieros. FACT in "1988" 6848 fiero GTs were made and 5298 had the wind option, BUT 1550 did not, something to think about before you drill that deck lid and put on a wing! <P>Later Fiero John (mine wingless 88 White GT)  <P>------------------<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000012||Jaei Sun||11-21-2001||06:52 PM||||Ya all need some aftermarket wheels on those!  Wingless fieros look too plain with the stockers.<P> <IMG SRC="http://home.mn.rr.com/fierojaei/white.jpg"> <P>------------------<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://home.mn.rr.com/fierojaei/Jaei_blue.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000013||fropuff||11-21-2001||06:53 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FIERO JOHN-WI:<BR><B>Hey fellow wing less fiero owners, just a little fact for you collector or hobbiests of fieros. FACT in "1988" 6848 fiero GTs were made and 5298 had the wind option, BUT 1550 did not, something to think about before you drill that deck lid and put on a wing! <P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>John, my decklid is for an '86 GT, and the only reason that I'm getting rid of it is because FieroMontreal wanted a replacement.  He isn't going to butcher it.  I just like the look of a wing better, so I'm going to buy a decklid with the holes already in there.  I know their rarity, but I don't really care about stockness.  I think I just made up two new words.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  So don't worry, I'm not drilling any holes.  BUMP for FieroMontreal.  Thanks.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000014||banditbalz||11-21-2001||07:03 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Jaei Sun:<BR><B>Ya all need some aftermarket wheels on those!  Wingless fieros look too plain with the stockers.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Ya all need some aftermarket springs... <P>Sorry Jaei Sun, that is one trick ride but you need to lower it 2 or 3 inches!<BR>You get those tinted quarter windows from Fiero warehouse or tint them yourself?<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/blackwhite2_3.jpg"> <P><P>------------------<BR>Silver 86 GT<BR>completely stock,<BR>completely fast!||||reg||1
Z||000015||Jaei Sun||11-21-2001||07:22 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Ya all need some aftermarket springs...<HR></BLOCKQUOTE> <P>Touche'  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>I had STs ready to install, but I sold them because I decide to go with Coil-overs in the back.  <P>The Quarter Windows are the fierowarehouse Replicas and they're fantastic.  Easy install and they even supplied the proper size double stick tape for installation.  I highly recommend them for anyone lookin for new quarter glass!||||reg||1
Z||000016||banditbalz||11-21-2001||07:27 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Jaei Sun:<BR><B> <BR>I had STs ready to install, but I sold them because I decide to go with Coil-overs in the back.  <BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I have Eibachs all around. Not happy with the rears. Also looking to go coil over in the rear. I also have Fiero warehouse quarter windows, but tint was not available at the time. Plan to buy a set of tinted this spring. I agree, the quality is excellent. Made of Acrylic (very flexible), not Lexan like the originals.<P><P>------------------<BR>Silver 86 GT<BR>completely stock,<BR>completely fast!||||reg||6
